# Pull requests: fork only (default)

Default PR target is the **fork** (`origin`), never public upstream `Project-MONAI/MONAI`.

## Must

- Resolve the fork before any `gh pr create`:
  `FORK=$(gh repo view --json nameWithOwner -q .nameWithOwner)`
  (or derive the same owner/repo from `git remote get-url origin`).
- Open draft PRs with an explicit fork repo flag:
  `gh pr create --draft --repo "$FORK" --base <base> --head <task-branch> ...`
- Before running `gh pr create`, print the exact command (repo + base + head) and confirm `$FORK` is the fork, not `Project-MONAI/MONAI`.
- Multiple bases on the fork are fine (`dev`, `cursor-onboarding`). A PR is a comparison (`--base <branch>`); do **not** merge, rebase, or pull that base into the task branch unless the human asks.
- If a PR was opened on the wrong repo: stop, tell the human, `gh pr close` it on that repo, open the correct fork PR. Closing does not delete the wrong PR — never leave it.

## Must not

- NEVER run `gh pr create` / `gh pr create --repo Project-MONAI/MONAI` (or any equivalent that opens a PR on upstream) unless the human **explicitly** asked for an upstream PR in this conversation.
- NEVER omit `--repo` when this clone has both `origin` (fork) and `upstream` — `gh` can target the wrong repository.
- NEVER push to `upstream`. That remote is fetch / read / compare / issues only.
- NEVER treat “open a second PR against `cursor-onboarding`” as a reason to merge `cursor-onboarding` into the head branch.

## Remotes

| Remote | Role |
|--------|------|
| `origin` | Fork — push and open PRs here |
| `upstream` | `Project-MONAI/MONAI` — read-only unless the human opts into an upstream PR |

Hard enforcement: `.cursor/hooks/deny-upstream-pr.py` on `beforeShellExecution` denies upstream-targeted `gh pr create` (and ambiguous creates missing `--repo`).
